# Gate of the ipu4-patches / ipu6 leg: the upstreamable driver under the
# IPU6 QEMU model. Owned by the IPU4 port; gains a test once it passes on
# the IPU6 baseline (enabled-tests.ipu6.ipu6) and here.
#
# One test name per line; '#' starts a comment. Every known test runs on
# every PR, but only the tests listed here fail the job; run
# `tools/tests/ipu6/ladder.sh --list` for the names.

# Static tests: the same tree as ipu4-patches / ipu4.
series-applies
build
checkpatch

# What the IPU6 baseline passes: the series does not break IPU6 probe,
# buttress power-up or the ISYS runtime resume.
vm-boot
module-load
probe-identify
probe-buttress
isys-resume

# PSYS MMU init and the ISYS resume's writes against the upstream driver's
# IPU6 tables, as on the baseline (ipu6 plan V7).
probe-mmu
isys-irq
